From 33ea90931049312a8ca6115f2387d1024a3e8896 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:20:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 04/51] port: devdax mapping at map_va, deterministic SCR/LNR
 arenas, init/attach

- PortContext (src/shared_memory/cxl_port.*): loads systems/common
  cxl_region.h, maps the whole device MAP_SHARED|MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE at
  map_va, control block in HWcc page 0 (magic, version, layout_hash,
  state EMPTY->INITIALIZING->READY, cursors, log_root, node_alive[2]).
  Node 0 requires EMPTY or reinit; node 1 waits for READY, checks
  version/layout_hash, write-protects HWcc/SWcc while attaching (default
  on), then checks its cursors and log_root against node 0's.
  Start barrier on node_alive before any NR write [C4].
  SCR footprint is checked against hwcc_size before mapping [V9].
- AllocatableLocalMemoryRegion: arena mode (bump allocator over the
  mapping, sealed after init/attach) and private-heap mode; memkind is no
  longer used.
- scr arena = HWcc minus the control page: shared counter block [V1],
  four SCR bitmaps, NR log header, WriteMetadata records. lnr arena =
  SWcc: CacheNode array, slot data, NR log entries.
- Attach skips every write of initial shared contents (bitmap memsets,
  WriteMetadata construct loop, CacheNode init loop, log construction).
- Handles (SharedMemoryObject and members, SharedMetadata, wmeta manager)
  are process-local; local seqcount maps on the private heap, for this
  node only. Shared arrays are never destroyed.
- [V1] allocated_slot_num_/reclaim_count_/allocate_count_ and
  SharedBitmap count_/dirty_count_ live in the shared counter block.
- Without DYN_WMETA every slot needs a record; refuse otherwise.
- One wmeta manager, on node 0 only; critical-path reclaim everywhere.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
